 {'chainIds': [196], 'lens': 'L1', 'check': 'Whether the global keccak cache in front of KECCAK256 on X Layer (alloy-primitives 1.6.0 keccak_cache.rs with fixed-cache 0.1.10) can return a hash for an input other than the one asked, which would change every pool, tick, position and delta slot the PoolManager computes (src/types/PoolId.sol:14 is 160 bytes and bypasses it; src/libraries/Position.sol:60 at 58 bytes, src/libraries/CurrencyDelta.sol:14 at 64 bytes and every compiler-generated mapping slot at 64 bytes go through it).', 'result': 'No. The key stores the length and the bytes, and equality compares the full slice (keccak_cache.rs lines 80-113). get_or_insert_with_ref locks the bucket only when its tag word equals the computed tag, compares the stored key with the input under that lock, and otherwise computes keccak256 of the input itself and inserts it (fixed-cache lib.rs get_inner, insert_inner and try_lock_ret, Acquire on lock and Release on unlock). An empty bucket has key length zero and the empty input never reaches the cache. A hash collision or a racing writer can only cause a miss. Any account can evict entries through eth_call or transactions, which changes speed only. 13,488 KECCAK256 vectors (every length 1 to 96 at eight offsets, inputs that share a prefix and differ only in length, all-zero and one-bit inputs, 64 byte mapping and 58 byte position shapes, each set sent twice so the second round hits a warm cache) returned the specified hash on f60420a, and 6,744 of them on Celo reth 74cc8bb, which has no cache: %s and %s mismatches.' % (kx['mismatchCount'] if kx else '?', kc['mismatchCount'] if kc else '?'), 'source': AP},
 {'chainIds': [42220, 196], 'lens': 'L4', 'check': 'The engine precompile cache (crates/engine/tree/src/tree/precompile_cache.rs) of okx/reth f60420a and celo-org/reth 74cc8bb, listed in OPCODES.md as unread: whether a cached result can be returned for a call the precompile would answer differently, or whether a stateful precompile is cached.', 'result': 'Entries are kept per precompile address, keyed by the full input bytes and filtered by spec; a hit also needs the caller gas to be at least the cached gas used, and only successful outputs that did not touch the reservoir or state gas are stored. The two files differ only in an initial_capacity line. map_cacheable_precompiles in alloy-evm 0.34.0 skips identity and any precompile marked stateful, and alloy-celo-evm marks the Celo transfer precompile with .stateful(), so a CELO token transfer always moves balances. The PoolManager reads no precompile result in its own math; a pool whose currency is the CELO token reaches the transfer precompile only through the token contract.', 'source': PC_OKX},
 {'chainIds': [42220], 'lens': 'L4', 'check': 'The two copies of the Celo transfer precompile: celo-revm precompiles/transfer.rs (handler path) and alloy-celo-evm lib.rs transfer_precompile (DynPrecompile path used by reth execution and eth_call), whose comment says they must be kept in sync.', 'result': 'Both halt in a static context, halt with out of gas below 9,000, require the caller to be the chain\'s CELO token, require exactly 96 bytes, read from, to and value from the same offsets, restore the cold status of from and to before Jovian, move value with the journal transfer and halt on a transfer or database error. No difference in order or bounds was found.', 'source': CTR},
 {'chainIds': [42220, 196], 'lens': 'L1', 'check': 'The keccak assembly behind KECCAK256: sha3-asm 0.1.6 (Celo) against 0.1.8 (X Layer), and which CRYPTOGAMS routine each released build assembles.', 'result': 'Both choose the routine at build time from target features. With the default x86_64 target, as in the Celo Dockerfile (RUSTFLAGS only adds frame pointers and line tables) and the X Layer DockerfileOp (empty RUSTFLAGS), both assemble keccak1600-x86_64. 0.1.8 changes symbol renaming for the _neon and _kimd suffixes, fixes patch matching by exact stem and puts Zen 5 on the plain routine; none of it changes the plain x86_64 routine. The battery KECCAK256 vectors and the 13,488 cache vectors exercise the endpoint build. The avx512vl routine a target-cpu=native build would choose was not executed; see the lead.', 'source': SHA8},
